wm2tj (0.1.0~beta8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj-bar: monitors chooses where the bar goes: primary (the
    default), all, or monitor names. The bar sits on the primary monitor
    and every other monitor chosen gets a copy whose clicks, tips and
    menus act as on the bar; menus stay inside the monitor. The bar
    follows XRandR changes. Builds with libxrandr.
  * wm2tj: maximize, fullscreen and the strip a dock keeps free are per
    monitor (XRandR): a window maximizes on its own monitor, not across
    all of them. A dock along the top or bottom edge of any monitor keeps
    that strip free, with or without a strut; left and right struts and
    panels count too. Monitors are followed as they change (XRandR, and
    the root's ConfigureNotify that xrandr --setmonitor sends); clones
    count once. Builds with libxrandr.
  * wm2tj: a new window the application did not place opens on the
    monitor the pointer is on (it opened on the first one), and windows,
    the root menu and the geometry box stay within one monitor.
  * wm2tj-bar: a bar or copy with no monitor above it reserves a strut
    over its own columns, so other window managers keep it free as well.
    Clones get one bar. Up to 16 monitors.
  * tests/multimonitor: an automatic test on a dummy Xorg (14 layouts:
    stacked, side by side, L-shaped, 2x2, portrait, mirrored, hotplug,
    side panels).
  * wm2tj-bar: the brightness keys and slider set every backlight of the
    best type together (a machine with two panels has two raw ones; only
    the first was set). backlight takes several names.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj: windows no longer end up under the top bar. The strip a dock
    reserves with _NET_WM_STRUT(_PARTIAL) is now off limits for every
    window, not only for placement and maximizing: dragging a window
    stops at the bar, an application that asks for a position under it
    is moved down, and windows already there are pushed down when a bar
    appears or grows. Without a bar the strip is free again. Fullscreen
    windows still cover the whole screen.
  * wm2tj publishes _NET_WORKAREA on the root window (the screen minus
    the struts, per desktop), so GTK and Qt place dialogs and popups
    clear of the bar.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj: the root menu is read again from ~/.wm2rc when the file has
    changed, as the menu opens, with no restart. Installing applications
    (wm2-menu-sync) or editing the favourites restarted wm2tj, which
    re-frames every window: the screen flickered and windows jumped for
    each app installed. Fonts, colours and frames still need SIGHUP.
  * wm2tj sets _WM2TJ_MENU_RELOAD on the root window; wm2-menu-gen --hup
    then sends no SIGHUP (an older wm2tj still gets one). The favourites
    editor and wm2tj-bar (sync_wm2tj) now leave the restart to
    wm2-menu-gen --hup.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:00:24 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj-bar: the .deb build compiled the bar with PREFIX=/usr/local, so
    it looked for its translations in /usr/local/share/locale and its menus
    came up in English. debian/rules now builds with PREFIX=/usr, and the
    bar is rebuilt whenever LOCALEDIR changes between make and make install.
  * wm2tj-bar --version prints the package version (0.1.0~beta5).

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:51:53 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj: a window that asks to be mapped while wm2tj restarts (such as a
    program started from the root menu, which holds a SIGHUP back until
    it closes) is no longer lost: pending map and configure requests are
    carried out before wm2tj lets go of the display, and the window comes
    up on top. The wallpaper chooser could fail to appear this way.
  * wm2-menu-gen: new --settle N (wait until the application dirs and the
    favourites have been quiet for N seconds) and --hup (restart wm2tj
    only when the menu changed; ~/.wm2rc is not rewritten when it would
    stay the same). wm2-menu-sync.service uses both, so installing many
    applications at once restarts wm2tj once instead of every few
    seconds.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:05:10 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj: keep the stacking order across a restart (SIGHUP). Windows were
    released in reverse creation order, which turned the stack over on
    every restart and could leave a settings window under the others.
  * wm2tj-favorites, wm2tj-bar: do not rebuild the menu and restart wm2tj
    themselves while wm2-menu-sync.path (systemd --user) watches the
    favourites file, so a change restarts wm2tj once instead of twice.
  * wm2tj-favorites: drop the raise after the restart (it had no effect);
    a hand-written comment after "new_label none" is no longer taken for
    the entry's name.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:48:17 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj-favorites: changes stay in the window until Apply (with Revert,
    and a question when closing with changes not applied), so wm2tj is
    restarted once per Apply instead of on every add, remove or move; the
    application list is updated in place instead of rebuilt; the window
    is raised again after wm2tj restarts.

